  <name>ExitCodesAndDiagnostics</name>
  <type>clidocumentation:ExitCodesAndDiagnostics</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>Exit codes and diagnostic formatting</is>

  <documentation>CLI18 exit codes:
    • 0 — success
    • 1 — compiler/parser/validator errors (diagnostics with severity error)
    • 2 — configuration error (unknown command, missing file, unsupported target, bootstrap failure)
      or uncaught Internal CLI error (application failure, not a BML diagnostic)

    CLI17 diagnostic format: severity code file:line — message
    Printed to stderr first. Then a status line:
    validate — Validation succeeded|failed. Tested N block(s), M with errors.
    compile — Compilation succeeded. Wrote …  |  Compilation failed with K error(s).
    Uncaught exception — Internal CLI error: message (exit 2; no stack dump).
    runCli joins lines with newlines.</documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidocumentation:DualCliModel" relation="ReadNext"></see>
  </references>

</block>
